=== how the 60 genes divide ===
  no fixed difference of any kind     : 28
  fixed differences, none amino-acid  : 12
  at least one amino-acid change      : 20

The manuscript reports 17 of 60 genes with no fixed difference at
all. This run gives 28, because a site is used here only when
the ingroup is strictly monomorphic and every ancestral codon position
reaches PP >= 0.9, which is stricter than the MK counting. Reconcile
the two before quoting either number.

=== OG0000120 dominates the amino-acid count ===
  it contributes Dn = 16 of 60 (27%)
  excluding it: Dn = 44, Ds = 59
  This is the OX-2/CD200 locus whose aBSREL signal the manuscript
  already attributes to a 29-codon unalignable block. Its
  substitutions are in the output table but should be reported
  separately, not pooled with the rest.

=== character of the 60 non-synonymous changes ===
  change physicochemical class : 34 (56.7%)
  conservative within class    : 26

  internal null: 143 non-synonymous changes segregating
  as polymorphism within LSDV (>= 5% minor allele), of which
  82 (57.3%) are radical

  fixed 56.7% vs polymorphic 57.3%  OR = 0.97, Fisher p = 1.000
  No difference. The fixed changes are no more radical than the
  ones still segregating, so this gives no additional evidence
  either way. Report it as such.

